# The moment (Docs/Design/62-talk.md, phase 7): the weather, the day, festivals, lore and where you're from, as
# chains. One remarks on the moment; the other answers as they are (moment.reply_weather, _day, _festival, _lore,
# _home: chosen by the answerer's job, home, age, means and temper); the first closes it (moment.close), in kind with
# what the answer was.
#
# Two pair memories carry the chain (two minutes: a chain's beats are chosen at once):
#   m7o  what kind of opener it was, where a reply has to know: need (cold, hungry, homeless), far (from elsewhere),
#        busy (working while others rest), pup (a pup's question), tale (lore), and for the day: market, stall, rest,
#        dawn, dusk, night, crowd, quiet, done (after a shift), dayoff. Replies keyed to it have priority, so a chain's
#        best tier always answers what was actually said.
#   m7   how the answer went, for the close: moan, glad, joke, work, poor, posh, weary, hungry, fear, boats, crowd,
#        gossip, home, local, prickly, gladgone, offer, same, snub, sorry, farre, together, tease, busy, topup,
#        pupchat, pupgift, scoff, believe, version, pious, spooked, oldtell, scholar, hometale.
# A reply with no m7 gets the plain closes. Mourning answers hand to keeping.sorry (k=grief).

# ================================================================ The weather: openers (talk.weather: outdoors only)

rule m7_wx_open_any
when concept=talk.weather
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say Look at it. Just look at it. | What do you make of this sky? | Strange weather for the time of year#tag#. | I can't make my mind up about today. | Funny old sky today.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_rain
when concept=talk.weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say It's coming down in rods. | My hood's given up. | Another day of this #rain#. | I've had drier baths. | I can feel it in my boots. | It's found its way down my collar. All of it.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_snow
when concept=talk.weather here.weather=snow
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say #snow.capitalize# up to my hocks already. | It's settling. That's the trouble, it's settling. | I can't feel my paw pads. | Everything's gone quiet under it. | Snowing again. Sideways, this time.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_fog
when concept=talk.weather here.weather=fog
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say I just begged a post's pardon. | You can taste this #fog#. | Can't see the end of my own tail. | Every sound's coming from the wrong side. | My whiskers are dripping.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_storm
when concept=talk.weather here.weather=storm
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say #oath#! Did you hear that one? Shook my teeth. | This #wind# wants the roofs off. | I counted three between the flash and the bang. | Something's come loose somewhere and it's banging like a drum. | Hold on to your hat.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_clear
when concept=talk.weather here.weather=clear here.time=dawn|day
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say Not a cloud. I don't trust it. | Now that's a sky. | Sun on my back for once. | You can see for miles today. | Look at that. Blue as a jay.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_clear_night
when concept=talk.weather here.weather=clear here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say Not a cloud. The owls'll be busy. | Look at that sky. You could count them all, if you'd the nights to spare. | Clear as a bell. The cold's coming down already. | Light enough to find the way home without a lamp.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_overcast
when concept=talk.weather here.weather=overcast
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say Grey as a pot lid. | It can't decide whether to rain. | The sky's sulking. | Heavy, isn't it? Like it's holding its breath. | No sun, no rain. Just grey.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_sandstorm
when concept=talk.weather here.weather=sandstorm
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say I've dust in places dust shouldn't be. | Cover your eyes. | Can't see the field for the dirt in the air. | It's in my teeth. Grit, all of it.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_dawn_frost
when concept=talk.weather here.time=dawn here.season=winter|autumn here.weather=clear|overcast
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say Frost on everything. The pump handle bit me. | White on the roofs this morning. | My breath's coming out in clouds. | The puddles have lids on.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_dusk_summer
when concept=talk.weather here.time=dusk here.season=summer here.weather=clear
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say Warm evening. The ground's still giving off the day. | Swifts screaming overhead. | Light till all hours, this time of year. | Lovely, this. Don't tell anyone I said so.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_night_rain
when concept=talk.weather here.time=night here.weather=rain|storm
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say Only fools and the watch out in this. | Black as a tar barrel, and wet with it. | I'll be dripping on the floor till morning. | Can't hear yourself think for it.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_spring_rain
when concept=talk.weather here.season=spring here.weather=rain|overcast
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say Green rain. You can smell things growing. | The buds won't mind it. | Smells of earth and wet blossom. | Every ditch has a song in it today.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_summer_heat
when concept=talk.weather here.season=summer here.time=day here.weather=clear here.region!=frosthollow
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say My tongue's out to my chin. | Too hot for fur. | The flies are the only ones enjoying this. | I've been panting since breakfast.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_autumn_wind
when concept=talk.weather here.season=autumn here.weather=overcast|storm|rain
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say Leaves everywhere. In my collar, even. | The #wind#'s got a bite to it now. | Summer's packed up and gone without a word. | Smell that? Woodsmoke and wet leaves.
then other: moment.reply_weather

# Openers by who's speaking: their work, their home, their age.

rule m7_wx_open_farmer_dry
when concept=talk.weather self.job=farmer|herder here.weather=clear here.season=summer
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say The ground's cracking. We want rain. | Lovely day if you're not a turnip. | Another dry one. The peas are curling up.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_farmer_wet
when concept=talk.weather self.job=farmer|herder here.weather=rain here.season=autumn
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say Can't get the last of it in. Not in this. | The stooks are sodden. | Rain at harvest. Every year the same prayer, and the same answer.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_fisher
when concept=talk.weather self.job=fisher|sailor here.weather=storm|fog
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say No boats out today. Not one. | I'd not take a rowboat across a puddle in this. | Somebody's out there in it. Somebody always is.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_guard
when concept=talk.weather self.job=guard|soldier here.weather=rain|snow|storm
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say Eight hours in this, and the captain wants the boots polished. | My mail's rusting as I stand here. | Nobody causes trouble in weather like this. Small mercies.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_carter
when concept=talk.weather self.job=carter here.weather=rain|snow|storm
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say The road'll be #mud# to the axles. | I've a load due by dusk and no hope of it. | Horses hate it. I hate it. We're agreed.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_old
when concept=talk.weather self.stage=old here.weather=rain|fog|overcast
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say My knees told me yesterday. | Weather's not what it was. Wetter. | Seventy years under this sky, and I like it less every one.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_young
when concept=talk.weather self.stage=young
does ask.detail
cooldown 1d
say {m7o=pup} Who makes the weather? | {m7o=pup} Why's the sky that colour? | {m7o=pup} Can clouds fall down? | {m7o=pup} Does the sky ever run out of weather?
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_south_in_snow
when concept=talk.weather here.weather=snow self.from=oakhaven|mirebridge|fenshore|larkfield|southmeadow
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say {m7o=far} Where I come from this is a story you tell pups. | {m7o=far} I didn't know cold went this deep. | {m7o=far} How do you live like this? Honestly. How?
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_north_in_heat
when concept=talk.weather here.region=south here.season=summer here.weather=clear self.from=frosthollow|coldwater
does ask.detail
cooldown 2d
say {m7o=far} Does the sun never go in, down here? | {m7o=far} Is it always this hot down here? | {m7o=far} My fur was made for snow, not this.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_city_rain_away
when concept=talk.weather here.weather=rain here.region!=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say Ah. Rain. Almost feels like home. | You call this rain? In Ridgemere we'd call it a dry spell. | Smells like the Sound, this.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_poor_cold
when concept=talk.weather self.wealth=destitute|poor here.season=winter here.weather=snow|rain|overcast|storm self.stage=adult|old
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
priority 1
say {m7o=need} No wood till Restday. We sleep in our coats. | {m7o=need} The damp's in the walls again. | {m7o=need} Cold's dearer for some than others.
then other: moment.reply_weather

rule m7_wx_open_homeless
when concept=talk.weather self.homeless=yes here.weather=rain|snow|storm
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
priority 2
say {m7o=need} Where'll I sleep tonight, in this? | {m7o=need} Every doorway's taken. | {m7o=need} I've been wet three days now. You stop noticing. Almost.
then other: moment.reply_weather

# ================================================================ The weather: answers (self is the one answering)

rule m7_wx_re_any
when concept=moment.reply_weather
does assess
say Could be worse. Could be raining frogs. | It'll change. It always does. | I've stopped looking up. Saves disappointment. | Weather's weather. You can't argue with it. | Mm. Same sky over all of us.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_any2
when concept=moment.reply_weather
does assess
say My mother said you can't eat weather, so stop chewing it. | It is what it is. | Keeps us talking, at least. | The sky doesn't ask our leave, does it?
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_rain
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=rain
does assess
say {m7=moan} Ducks are happy. Someone ought to be. | {m7=moan} The water butt's full, so that's one thing. | {m7=moan} Washes the fleas out, I suppose. | {m7=moan} #annoyed#. Wet as a fish's elbow.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_snow
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=snow
does assess
say It'll be grey slush by noon. | Pretty for an hour. Then it's just #cold#. | Mind the eaves. They drop it on you. | If a snowball finds you later, it wasn't me.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_fog
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=fog
does assess
say Keep to the path. | I heard the cart before I saw it. Nearly lost a tail. | Fog's good for one thing: nobody sees you yawn. | It'll lift. Or we'll all wander off and get lost.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_storm
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=storm
does assess
say {m7=fear} Inside, and quick about it. | {m7=fear} I've tied everything down that'll tie. | {m7=fear} The Dark One's moving the furniture. | {m7=fear} That one was close. Too close.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_clear
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=clear here.time=dawn|day
does assess
say {m7=glad} Make the most of it. That's #luck#, that is. | {m7=glad} Washing day, then. | {m7=glad} Don't say it out loud. You'll scare it off. | {m7=glad} I'll take it. I'll take every scrap of it.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_clear_night
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=clear here.time=dusk|night
does assess
say No cloud to keep the warmth in. It'll bite tonight. | Stars thick as frost. | Pretty. Cold, but pretty. | I'll want two blankets.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_overcast
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=overcast
does assess
say It'll rain before long. | It's thinking about it. | Grey's restful, if you let it be. | No shadows, at least. Can't see your own gloom.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_sandstorm
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=sandstorm
does assess
say Shut your mouth and walk. | It'll blow through. | Keep a wet cloth over your nose.
then other: moment.close

# By their work.

rule m7_wx_re_farmer_rain
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=farmer|herder here.weather=rain here.season=spring|summer
does assess
cooldown 1d
say {m7=glad} Don't curse it. That's bread falling. | {m7=glad} My fields have been begging for this. | {m7=glad} Every drop's a loaf in the autumn.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_farmer_harvest_rain
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=farmer|herder here.weather=rain|storm here.season=autumn
does assess
cooldown 1d
say {m7=work} Half my barley's still standing out in it. | {m7=work} It'll sprout in the stook if it keeps on. | {m7=work} I've stopped looking at the sky. It only laughs.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_farmer_snow
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=farmer|herder here.weather=snow
does assess
cooldown 1d
say {m7=work} I was up before light digging the ewes out. | {m7=work} Snow's a blanket for the winter wheat. | {m7=work} The beasts want feeding whatever falls.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_fisher_fog
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=fisher|sailor here.weather=fog
does assess
cooldown 1d
say {m7=boats} No boat goes out in this. Not if they want to come back. | {m7=boats} Fog on the water's the worst. You row in circles. | {m7=boats} I've lost the shore in fog once. Never again.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_fisher_storm
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=fisher|sailor here.weather=storm|rain
does assess
cooldown 1d
say {m7=boats} I've doubled the lines on the boat. | {m7=boats} The water's white out there. Nobody's fool enough. | {m7=boats} Wind's the killer, not the wet.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_fisher_clear
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=fisher|sailor here.weather=clear
does assess
cooldown 1d
say {m7=joke} Flat water. Good for the nets. | {m7=joke} Clear sky, cold night. Fish go deep. | {m7=joke} I should be out. Why am I talking to you?
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_guard
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=guard|soldier here.weather=rain|snow|storm|fog
does assess
cooldown 1d
say {m7=work} I'm on the wall in it tonight. Lucky me. | {m7=work} Thieves stay in when it's like this. So should I. | {m7=work} My cloak's been wet since Dawnday.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_carter
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=carter here.weather=rain|snow|storm
does assess
cooldown 1d
say {m7=work} The roads'll be ruined. Three days late, everything. | {m7=work} My wheels will be #mud# to the hub. | {m7=work} I've a horse with a cough and a load of slate. Wish me luck.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_carter_fog
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=carter here.weather=fog
does assess
cooldown 1d
say {m7=work} I'll walk at the horse's head all the way, in this. | {m7=work} Last fog I drove the cart into a hedge. The hedge won. | {m7=work} Can't see the ruts. I'll feel for them.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_miner
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=miner
does assess
cooldown 1d
say {m7=joke} I'll be under the hill soon. It's always the same weather down there. | {m7=joke} Sun, snow, it's all one in the dark. | {m7=joke} Lucky you, to care what the sky does.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_smith_cold
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=smith here.season=winter
does assess
cooldown 1d
say {m7=joke} Come and stand by my forge. Warmest spot in town. | {m7=joke} I've the only warm paws for a mile. | {m7=joke} Everyone's my friend in winter. Funny, that.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_smith_heat
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=smith|baker|cook here.season=summer here.weather=clear here.region!=frosthollow
does assess
cooldown 1d
say {m7=work} Try a day by the fire in this. | {m7=work} I've been baking along with the bread. | {m7=work} I'd trade you for the shade.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_innkeeper_wet
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=innkeeper|brewer here.weather=rain|snow|storm
does assess
cooldown 1d
say {m7=joke} Good for trade. Wet wolves want a fire and a jar. | {m7=joke} I shouldn't say it, but I love a wet night. Full house. | {m7=joke} Keep it coming, I say. My taproom thanks it.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_merchant_wet
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.role=merchant here.weather=rain|storm|snow
does assess
cooldown 1d
say {m7=moan} Nobody buys when they're wet. | {m7=moan} My awning's a waterfall. | {m7=moan} I've sold one thing all day, and that was a hood.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_healer_winter
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=healer here.season=winter|autumn
does assess
cooldown 1d
say {m7=work} Every chest in town's rattling. I'm run off my paws. | {m7=work} Wrap up. I've no room for one more cough. | {m7=work} Cold brings me trade I'd rather not have.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_priest
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=priest
does assess
cooldown 1d
say We take what's sent, and give thanks for a roof. | The Bright One sends weather on the deserving and the rest alike. | Weather keeps us humble.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_woodcutter_storm
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=woodcutter here.weather=storm
does assess
cooldown 1d
say {m7=work} I'll be clearing windfall for a week. | {m7=work} Trees down everywhere tomorrow, you watch. | {m7=work} Never stand under an old tree in a #wind# like this.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_laborer_heat
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=laborer|miner|woodcutter here.season=summer here.weather=clear here.time=day here.region!=frosthollow
does assess
cooldown 1d
say {m7=work} I've hauled sacks since dawn in it. My tongue's dragging. | {m7=work} Try carrying stone in this. | {m7=work} Water. I need water and a cellar.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_beggar
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.job=beggar here.weather=rain|snow|storm
does assess
cooldown 1d
priority 1
say {m7=poor} Easy for some to talk about it. | {m7=poor} Spare a copper for a dry crust? | {m7=poor} Wet through, and the day not half done.
then other: moment.close

# By their home: the weather as it falls on one from elsewhere.

rule m7_wx_re_south_snow
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=snow self.from=oakhaven|mirebridge|fenshore|larkfield|southmeadow
does assess
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say {m7=home} Back home we'd be mending fences in our shirtsleeves. | {m7=home} At home I'd only seen snow on the far hills. Now it's in my boots. | {m7=home} I keep thinking it'll stop. It never stops.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_south_cold
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.season=winter here.region=north self.from=southmeadow|larkfield|oakhaven
does assess
cooldown 1d
say {m7=home} Winter down south is a brisk autumn up here. | {m7=home} I've worn every coat I own. At once. | {m7=home} My blood's too thin for the north. Always was.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_north_snow
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=snow self.from=frosthollow
does assess
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say {m7=joke} Call this snow? Up the valley it's to the eaves. | {m7=joke} This is a dusting. Come back when you can't find the door. | {m7=joke} Snow's a friend if you know it. Treat it right.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_north_heat
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.season=summer here.weather=clear self.from=frosthollow|coldwater here.region!=frosthollow|coldwater
does assess
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say {m7=home} Up home there'd still be snow in the gullies. I'd give a week's wage to roll in it. | {m7=home} I'm cooking in my own fur. | {m7=home} Glasswater would be cold enough to stop your heart right now. Lovely.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_fen_fog
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=fog self.from=mirebridge|fenshore
does assess
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say {m7=joke} This? In the fens this is a clear morning. | {m7=joke} Fog's only air with something to say. | {m7=joke} You learn to walk by smell in the fens.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_city_rain
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=rain self.from=ridgemere
does assess
cooldown 1d
say {m7=joke} I'm Ridgemere born. Rain's just air you can see. | {m7=joke} In Ridgemere we don't call it rain unless it's sideways. | {m7=joke} Rain doesn't count till it's coming up off the cobbles.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_lake_clear
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=clear|overcast self.from=coldwater here.region!=coldwater|ridgemere
does assess
cooldown 1d
say {m7=home} On a day like this Glasswater goes still as a plate. I miss it. | {m7=home} Nothing here to look into. At home you'd see your face in the lake. | {m7=home} I keep looking for the water and finding walls.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_downs_wind
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=overcast|storm self.from=larkfield here.region!=larkfield
does assess
cooldown 1d
say {m7=home} On the downs you'd feel this wind coming a day off. | {m7=home} I miss a good wind across open grass. Here it just whistles round corners. | {m7=home} Larks'd be up in this at home, singing into it.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_wood_rain
when concept=moment.reply_weather here.weather=rain self.from=oakhaven here.region!=oakhaven
does assess
cooldown 1d
say {m7=home} Under the Rainwood you'd barely feel it. The leaves take it all. | {m7=home} Rain's nicer with a roof of oak over you. | {m7=home} I miss the smell of wet leaf mould. Sounds daft.
then other: moment.close

# By age, means and mood.

rule m7_wx_re_old_bones
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.stage=old here.weather=rain|fog|snow|overcast
does assess
cooldown 1d
say My hip told me this a day ago. Hip's never wrong. | I've seen worse. I've seen the winter the wells froze solid. | At my age you're grateful for any weather you wake up to.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_young_snow
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.stage=young here.weather=snow
does assess
cooldown 1d
say {m7=glad} Can we build a snow fort? A big one? | {m7=glad} I ate some. It tastes of nothing. | {m7=glad} I'm going to slide down the lane on my tail!
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_young_rain
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.stage=young here.weather=rain|storm
does assess
cooldown 1d
say Puddles! The big one by the well's up to my knees! | Is the thunder angry at us? | I'm not cold. I'm not. My teeth just do that.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_adolescent
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.stage=adolescent
does assess
cooldown 1d
say {m7=joke} Who cares? It's weather. | {m7=joke} Can we not talk about the weather? Please? | {m7=joke} Everyone always talks about the weather. Every single day.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_poor
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.wealth=destitute|poor here.weather=rain|snow|storm here.season=autumn|winter self.stage=adult|old
does assess
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say {m7=poor} The roof's leaking over the bed again. | {m7=poor} I can't buy wood and bread both this week. | {m7=poor} We'll huddle. We always huddle.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_rich
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.wealth=rich here.weather=rain|snow|storm self.stage=adult|old
does assess
cooldown 1d
say {m7=posh} I've had the fires lit in every room. | {m7=posh} The carriage leaks, if you can believe it. | {m7=posh} Tiresome. I'll stay in and read.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_tired
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.tired=yes
does assess
cooldown 1d
say {m7=weary} I'm too #tired# to mind what the sky does. | {m7=weary} Rain, shine, I'll sleep through it given half a chance. | {m7=weary} Don't care. I want #bed#.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_mourning
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.mourning=kin|friend
does assess
priority 2
cooldown 1d
say {k=grief} I hadn't noticed. I don't notice much this week. | {k=grief} They'd have had something to say about it. They always did. | {k=grief} Is it? I've not looked up in days.
then other: keeping.sorry

rule m7_wx_re_dry
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.humour=dry self.stage!=young
does assess
cooldown 1d
say {m7=joke} Remarkable. Weather, happening, outdoors. | {m7=joke} Next you'll tell me it's dark at night. | {m7=joke} I'll write to the Council. They'll sort it.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_merry_wet
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.humour=merry here.weather=rain|storm|snow|fog
does assess
cooldown 1d
say {m7=joke} Lovely day for a duck! Or a fish. Or a wet wolf. | {m7=joke} I've given up being dry. It's very freeing. | {m7=joke} Sky's having a worse day than us, and that's saying something.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_merry_fair
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.humour=merry here.weather=clear|overcast
does assess
cooldown 1d
say {m7=joke} I'd sing, but I'd frighten the birds. | {m7=joke} Weather like this, I could dance. Don't hold me to it. | {m7=joke} Grand. Somebody fetch the cider.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_short
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.temper=short
does assess
cooldown 1d
say Talking about it won't change it. | #agree#, I can see it. I've got eyes. | #bc_and_q#
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_quiet
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.talk=quiet
does assess
cooldown 1d
say Mm. | Aye. | #bc_it_is#
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_devout
when concept=moment.reply_weather self.piety=devout here.weather=storm|snow|rain
does assess
cooldown 1d
say I'll light a candle for the ones out in it. | Pray for the boats and the shepherds. | It's sent. We bear it.
then other: moment.close

# A pup's question about the sky (m7o=pup).

rule m7_wx_re_to_pup
when concept=moment.reply_weather conv.m7o=pup self.stage=adult|old
does assess
priority 3
say {m7=topup} Ask a shepherd. They talk to it all day. | {m7=topup} The Bright One sends it. Don't ask me why. | {m7=topup} Because it can, pup. Same as you. | {m7=topup} Never yet, and I've been watching a long while.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_to_pup_merry
when concept=moment.reply_weather conv.m7o=pup self.stage=adult|old self.humour=merry|dry
does assess
priority 3
say {m7=topup} There's a wolf on the hill with a great bellows. Blows it all our way. | {m7=topup} Somebody up there's washing their blankets. | {m7=topup} Ask the clouds. They never tell me anything.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_wx_re_pup_pup
when concept=moment.reply_weather conv.m7o=pup self.stage=young|adolescent
does assess
priority 3
say {m7=pupchat} Dunno. Ask a grown-up. | {m7=pupchat} My brother says the sky's a big lake upside down. | {m7=pupchat} From the mountains. Everything bad comes from the mountains.
then other: moment.close

# ================================================================ Answering the opener's own plight (any of the moment's
# answers): in need (m7o=need), far from home (m7o=far), working while others rest (m7o=busy). Priority 3, so the
# answer meets what was said.

rule m7_re_need
when concept=moment.reply_weather|moment.reply_day|moment.reply_festival conv.m7o=need
does answer.how
priority 3
say {m7=sorry} #bad.capitalize# times. Harder for some. | {m7=sorry} The chapel gives out bread on Restday. Go early. | {m7=sorry} I'm sorry. I truly am. | {m7=sorry} It won't always be like this. It can't be.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_re_need_warm
when concept=moment.reply_weather|moment.reply_day|moment.reply_festival conv.m7o=need self.warmth=warm self.wealth!=destitute|poor self.stage=adult|old
does answer.how
priority 3
say {m7=offer} Come to ours tonight. There's a fire and a pot, and room for you. | {m7=offer} Here. Don't argue. Take it. | {m7=offer} You'll eat with us. That's settled. Bring whoever's yours.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_re_need_rich
when concept=moment.reply_weather|moment.reply_day|moment.reply_festival conv.m7o=need self.wealth=rich self.stage=adult|old
does answer.how
priority 3
say {m7=offer} Here. For wood. No, I insist. | {m7=offer} Take this. Buy something hot. | {m7=offer} I'll have something sent round. See that it is.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_re_need_poor
when concept=moment.reply_weather|moment.reply_day|moment.reply_festival conv.m7o=need self.wealth=destitute|poor
does answer.how
priority 3
say {m7=same} Same boat, you and me. Leaking the same. | {m7=same} We'll share what there is. Which is nothing, twice. | {m7=same} Don't I know it.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_re_need_cold
when concept=moment.reply_weather|moment.reply_day|moment.reply_festival conv.m7o=need self.warmth=cold self.stage=adult|old
does answer.how
priority 3
say {m7=snub} Should've put some by. | {m7=snub} Everyone's got troubles. | {m7=snub} Work harder, then.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_re_need_pup
when concept=moment.reply_weather|moment.reply_day|moment.reply_festival conv.m7o=need self.stage=young
does answer.how
priority 3
say {m7=pupgift} You can have half my bread. Here. | {m7=pupgift} My mum'll let you sit by our fire. Probably. | {m7=pupgift} I've got a penny. You can have it.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_re_far
when concept=moment.reply_weather|moment.reply_day|moment.reply_festival conv.m7o=far
does answer.how
priority 3
say {m7=farre} You'll get used to it. Everyone does. | {m7=farre} Give it a year. It'll be home before you know it. | {m7=farre} Miss it, do you? | {m7=farre} Bit different from home, eh?
then other: moment.close

rule m7_re_far_same
when concept=moment.reply_weather|moment.reply_day|moment.reply_festival conv.m7o=far pair.same_from=yes
does answer.how
priority 3
say {m7=together} Don't. I'll start missing it too. | {m7=together} I know. I think of it every day. | {m7=together} One day we'll both go back. You'll see.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_re_far_local
when concept=moment.reply_weather|moment.reply_day|moment.reply_festival conv.m7o=far self.from=frosthollow|coldwater here.region=frosthollow|coldwater here.weather=snow
does answer.how
priority 3
say {m7=tease} Soft. You're soft. You'll harden up. | {m7=tease} This is mild. Wait till midwinter. | {m7=tease} Wrap up and stop whining. We'll make a mountain wolf of you.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_re_busy
when concept=moment.reply_day|moment.reply_festival|moment.reply_weather conv.m7o=busy
does answer.how
priority 3
say {m7=busy} Somebody has to, I suppose. | {m7=busy} Don't let them work you into the ground. | {m7=busy} Shall I bring you something? A pie? | {m7=busy} You'll rest when it's done.
then other: moment.close

# ================================================================ Closing (self is the one who began), by how it went

rule m7_close_any
when concept=moment.close
does ack
say Well. There it is. | #farewell#. | Ah well. | I'll let you get on. | So it goes.
weight 1.5

rule m7_close_any2
when concept=moment.close
does ack
say #saying#. | #bc_true_enough# | Can't argue with that. | Mm. Well, then.

rule m7_close_dry
when concept=moment.close self.humour=dry !conv.m7
does ack
say Riveting. | We should do this more often. Or less. | Well, that's the day's excitement. | I'll treasure this talk.

rule m7_close_quiet
when concept=moment.close self.talk=quiet !conv.m7
does ack
say Mm. | Aye. | ...Aye. | Mm. Right.

rule m7_close_moan
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=moan
does ack
priority 1
say Chin up. It can't last for ever. | It'll pass. Most things do. | Aye, well. We'll live.

rule m7_close_moan_warm
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=moan self.warmth=warm
does ack
priority 1
say Come by mine later. There's a fire and a pot on. | Tomorrow'll be better. I'll see that it is. | Cheer up, #address#. I'll stand you something hot.

rule m7_close_glad
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=glad
does ack
priority 1
say That's the spirit. | Ha. You've cheered me up. | Let's have more days like this, then.

rule m7_close_joke
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=joke
does ack
priority 1
say Ha! | Get away with you. | You're no help at all. | I walked into that one.

rule m7_close_work
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=work
does ack
priority 1
say Rather you than me. | Don't let it grind you down. | #oath#, and I thought I had it bad.

rule m7_close_work_adult
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=work self.stage=adult|old
does ack
priority 1
say Rather you than me. | Don't let it grind you down. | I'll stand you #drink# when it's done. | #oath#, and I thought I had it bad.

rule m7_close_fear
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=fear
does ack
priority 1
say Stay safe. | Get indoors, then. Both of us. | Mind the slates going home.

rule m7_close_boats
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=boats
does ack
priority 1
say Bright One keep them that are out on it. | Stay ashore, then. | I'll not go near the water today.

rule m7_close_crowd
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=crowd
does ack
priority 1
say Go on, then. I'll find you after. | Stick by me. I'll get us through. | Breathe. It thins out by the well.

rule m7_close_gossip
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=gossip
does ack
priority 1
say Go on, then. Who? | Tell me at the well. I've a pot on. | Save it. I'll want all of it later.

rule m7_close_weary
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=weary
does ack
priority 1
say Get to your bed, then. | Go on home. Sleep. | You look it, if you don't mind my saying.

rule m7_close_hungry
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=hungry
does ack
priority 1
say Go and eat, for pity's sake. | Then go and find a pie. | I can hear it from here.

rule m7_close_posh
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=posh
does ack
priority 1
say Well. I'm sure you'll manage. | Hard lives, some of us. | Mm. Terrible for you.

rule m7_close_posh_poor
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=posh self.wealth=destitute|poor
does ack
priority 1
say My heart bleeds. | We should all have your troubles. | A leaky carriage. Bright One help us.

rule m7_close_posh_rich
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=posh self.wealth=rich
does ack
priority 1
say I know. One suffers. | Quite. Quite. | Ours has been the same. Dreadful.

rule m7_close_poor
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=poor
does ack
priority 1
say That's hard. I'm sorry. | It'll mend. Things do. | Hard times, these.

rule m7_close_poor_warm
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=poor self.warmth=warm self.wealth!=destitute|poor
does ack
priority 1
say Come by ours. There's always a bowl. | Here. Take this, and no arguing. | Don't you sleep out tonight. You hear me?

rule m7_close_poor_poor
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=poor self.wealth=destitute|poor
does ack
priority 1
say Two leaky boats, then. | We'll keep each other afloat. | Ha. Misery loves company.

rule m7_close_poor_cold
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=poor self.warmth=cold
does ack
priority 1
say Hm. Well. | Hard times all round. | The chapel takes folk in, I hear.

rule m7_close_poor_rich
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=poor self.wealth=rich
does ack
priority 1
say The chapel does good work, I'm told. | Ah. Well. One hears it's dreadful. | I'll mention it to someone.

rule m7_close_offer
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=offer
does ack
priority 2
say I... #thanks#. Truly. | Bless you. I'll not forget it. | You're too good. I'll pay you back. Somehow.

rule m7_close_pupgift
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=pupgift
does ack
priority 2
say Keep your bread, little one. But bless you for it. | You're a good pup. Your mother raised you right. | Ha. I'll hold you to that.

rule m7_close_same
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=same
does ack
priority 2
say Two leaky boats, then. | We'll keep each other afloat. | Ha. Misery loves company.

rule m7_close_sorry
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=sorry
does ack
priority 2
say Aye. Well. | Kind of you to say. | We'll manage. We always do.

rule m7_close_snub
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=snub
does ack
priority 2
say #annoyed#. Thanks for nothing. | I'll remember that. | Easy for you to say.

rule m7_close_farre
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=farre
does ack
priority 2
say So they keep telling me. | I hope you're right. | Some days more than others.

rule m7_close_together
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=together
does ack
priority 2
say One day. | Till then, there's two of us. | Aye. Together.

rule m7_close_tease
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=tease
does ack
priority 2
say I'll never be a mountain wolf. | Harden up yourself. | Bright One help me.

rule m7_close_busy
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=busy
does ack
priority 2
say Aye. Back to it. | Don't tempt me to stop. | It won't do itself, more's the pity.

rule m7_close_home
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=home other.home_here!=yes
does ack
priority 1
say Long way from home, then. | Tell me about it some time. Properly. | I'd like to see it one day. | You're here now, any road.

rule m7_close_home_cold
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=home self.warmth=cold other.home_here!=yes
does ack
priority 1
say Nobody made you come. | Go back, then. | Everyone's from somewhere.

rule m7_close_local
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=local
does ack
priority 1
say So it's me that talks funny. Fair enough. | I'll pick it up. Give me a year. | Then I'd best mind my own voice.

rule m7_close_prickly
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=prickly
does ack
priority 1
say No offence meant. | Touchy. | Suit yourself.

rule m7_close_gladgone
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=gladgone
does ack
priority 1
say Can't blame you. | Their loss, then. | Ha. Fair enough.

rule m7_close_topup
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=topup
does ack
priority 2
say I'm going to ask my mum. | That's not what Brindle says. | Promise? | I knew it!

rule m7_close_pupchat
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=pupchat
does ack
priority 2
say You're making it up. | I'm telling everyone. | Race you to the corner!

rule m7_close_market
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=market
does ack
priority 1
say Ha. Mind your purse. | I'll look out for you in the crush. | Save me a pie if you get there first.

rule m7_close_rest
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=rest
does ack
priority 1
say Wise words. | Ha. Right you are. | Don't remind me.

rule m7_close_dawn
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=dawn
does ack
priority 1
say I'll leave you to wake up, then. | Go on. Off you go. | Same here, if I'm honest.

rule m7_close_night
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=night
does ack
priority 1
say Ha. Same as you, then. | Mind the watch doesn't take you for a thief. | Well. Don't stay out too late.

rule m7_close_done
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=done
does ack
priority 1
say That's the plan. | I will. Don't work too hard. | Home, and nothing till morning.

rule m7_close_both
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=both
does ack
priority 1
say Come on, then. First round's mine. | Aye. Let's sit a while. | Not a word about work. Agreed.

rule m7_close_dayoff
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=dayoff
does ack
priority 1
say I'll try. It doesn't come natural. | Lucky? I'll be bored by noon. | I mean to.

rule m7_close_teen
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=teen
does ack
priority 1
say Ha. I remember being your age. | Go on, then. Enjoy it. | Mind your manners, mind.

# Lore closes (the one who told the tale).

rule m7_close_scoff
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=scoff
does ack
priority 1
say Laugh all you like. | Believe what you want. My grandmother did. | Well, that's how I heard it. | You'll see. One of these nights.

rule m7_close_believe
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=believe
does ack
priority 1
say Keep a lamp lit tonight, then. | See? It's not just me. | Sleep well. Ha.

rule m7_close_version
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=version
does ack
priority 1
say Every hearth tells it its own way. | Yours sounds worse. I'll keep mine. | Tell me yours some night. With the lamp low.

rule m7_close_pious
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=pious
does ack
priority 1
say No harm in a tale. | Aye, well. It's still a good tale. | I'll say a prayer as well, then. To be safe.

rule m7_close_spooked
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=spooked
does ack
priority 1
say It's only a tale! Come back! | I'll walk you to your door, if you like. | Ha! Sleep with a lamp lit, then.

rule m7_close_oldtell
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=oldtell
does ack
priority 1
say Go on, then. I've time. | Another night. I'll bring the ale. | I'll hold you to that.

rule m7_close_scholar
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=scholar
does ack
priority 1
say You've no romance in you. | Smaller and duller. That's learning for you. | Read it me some time, then.

rule m7_close_hometale
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=hometale
does ack
priority 1
say Every place has its own way of telling it. | I'd like to hear your way some night. | Same tale, different mud.

rule m7_close_tale_devout
when concept=moment.close conv.m7=scoff|believe|version|hometale self.piety=devout
does ack
priority 1
say The Bright One keeps us, tales or no. | I'll light a candle tonight all the same. | Tales are tales. Prayers are better.

# ================================================================ The day: openers (talk.day: two who know each other)

rule m7_day_open_any
when concept=talk.day
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say Where's the day gone? | Feels like a long one already. | Is it only #here.weekday#? | Funny sort of day#tag#. | Days are getting away from me.
then other: moment.reply_day

rule m7_day_open_market
when concept=talk.day here.day=market
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say {m7o=market} Marketday. The whole town's out with its purse. | {m7o=market} Have you been round the stalls yet? | {m7o=market} I've been elbowed three times and I've bought nothing. | {m7o=market} Market crowd's thick as porridge today.
then other: moment.reply_day

rule m7_day_open_rest
when concept=talk.day here.day=rest
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say {m7o=rest} Restday at last. My paws thank the Bright One. | {m7o=rest} Quiet, isn't it? You can hear the birds. | {m7o=rest} I don't know what to do with myself on a Restday. | {m7o=rest} Nothing to do but sit. Lovely.
then other: moment.reply_day

rule m7_day_open_work
when concept=talk.day here.day=work here.time=dawn
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say {m7o=dawn} Up with the birds again. | {m7o=dawn} Another day, another sack. | {m7o=dawn} #here.weekday.capitalize#, and already I'm counting to Restday.
then other: moment.reply_day

rule m7_day_open_dusk
when concept=talk.day here.time=dusk
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say {m7o=dusk} Lamps going on. Day's done. | {m7o=dusk} That's the light gone. | {m7o=dusk} Home, supper, #bed#. In that order. | {m7o=dusk} Long shadows. My favourite hour.
then other: moment.reply_day

rule m7_day_open_night
when concept=talk.day here.time=night
does ask.detail
cooldown 1d
say {m7o=night} What are you doing out at this hour? | {m7o=night} You're up late. | {m7o=night} Can't sleep either? | {m7o=night} Late to be wandering, isn't it?
then other: moment.reply_day

rule m7_day_open_crowd
when concept=talk.day here.crowd=crowd
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say {m7o=crowd} Where's everyone come from? | {m7o=crowd} Can't swing a cat for wolves today. | {m7o=crowd} Mind your purse in this crush.
then other: moment.reply_day

rule m7_day_open_quiet
when concept=talk.day here.crowd=quiet here.place=street|market
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say {m7o=quiet} Dead quiet. Where is everybody? | {m7o=quiet} Just you and me and the pigeons. | {m7o=quiet} Quiet as a chapel out here.
then other: moment.reply_day

rule m7_day_open_rest_working
when concept=talk.day here.day=rest self.working=yes
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say {m7o=busy} Restday, they call it. Not for me. | {m7o=busy} Somebody has to work while the rest of you pray. | {m7o=busy} I'll rest when I'm dead. Or Hearthday.
then other: moment.reply_day

rule m7_day_open_market_merchant
when concept=talk.day here.day=market self.role=merchant
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say {m7o=stall} Good day for it. I've sold out of half the stall. | {m7o=stall} They're haggling like it's a sport. | {m7o=stall} Marketday's the only day that pays the rent.
then other: moment.reply_day

rule m7_day_open_after_shift
when concept=talk.day self.shift=after
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say {m7o=done} That's me done. Done, done, done. | {m7o=done} Off my feet, finally. | {m7o=done} Day's work's behind me. Don't mention it.
then other: moment.reply_day

rule m7_day_open_day_off
when concept=talk.day self.shift=day_off
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say {m7o=dayoff} Day off. I keep thinking I've forgotten something. | {m7o=dayoff} Nothing to do and all day to do it. | {m7o=dayoff} I slept till the bells. Shameless.
then other: moment.reply_day

# ================================================================ The day: answers (self is the one answering)

# To a remark on the day as such (no m7o).

rule m7_day_re_any
when concept=moment.reply_day
does answer.how
say Same as ever. One foot, then the other. | I've stopped counting them. | Another day closer to something. | Aye. There's always tomorrow. | Days are like beans. All the same till you need one.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_any2
when concept=moment.reply_day
does answer.how
say Can't complain. Well, I can. | Mustn't grumble, so I won't. Much. | It's had its moments. | So far, so ordinary.
then other: moment.close

# To the opener's kind of day (priority 1).

rule m7_day_re_market
when concept=moment.reply_day conv.m7o=market
does answer.how
priority 1
say {m7=market} Once round. The prices'd make you weep. | {m7=market} I'm keeping my purse in my teeth. | {m7=market} I'm only here for the cheese. | {m7=market} Thick as porridge, and twice as slow.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_market_merchant
when concept=moment.reply_day conv.m7o=market self.role=merchant
does answer.how
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say {m7=work} I've not sat down since dawn. Don't keep me. | {m7=work} Busy's good. Busy's rent. | {m7=work} One more haggler and I'll give it away to be rid of them.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_market_poor
when concept=moment.reply_day conv.m7o=market self.wealth=destitute|poor self.stage=adult|old
does answer.how
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say {m7=poor} I look. Looking's free. | {m7=poor} Smelled the pies. That'll do me. | {m7=poor} I've a penny and a list as long as my tail.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_market_young
when concept=moment.reply_day conv.m7o=market self.stage=young
does answer.how
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say {m7=glad} There's a wolf with a dancing bird! A real one! | {m7=glad} I'm allowed one honey cake. Just one. | {m7=glad} I lost my mother twice already.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_stall
when concept=moment.reply_day conv.m7o=stall
does answer.how
priority 1
say {m7=joke} Then you can stand me a pie. | {m7=joke} Good. Your prices can come down, then. | {m7=joke} Glad somebody's doing well out of it.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_stall_merchant
when concept=moment.reply_day conv.m7o=stall self.role=merchant
does answer.how
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say Lucky you. Mine's been dead as a doornail. | Same here. My voice is gone from crying my wares. | Don't boast. It brings the tax-farmers.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_rest
when concept=moment.reply_day conv.m7o=rest
does answer.how
priority 1
say {m7=rest} Rest while you can. | {m7=rest} I've done nothing all morning, and I'm proud of it. | {m7=rest} Sit. That's the whole trick of it. | {m7=rest} It won't last. Dawnday's coming.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_rest_devout
when concept=moment.reply_day conv.m7o=rest self.piety=devout
does answer.how
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say {m7=rest} I've been to chapel twice. I'll go again at dusk. | {m7=rest} Rest's a gift. You should take it. | {m7=rest} A good sermon this morning. You missed it.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_rest_working
when concept=moment.reply_day conv.m7o=rest self.working=yes
does answer.how
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say {m7=work} Easy for you. I've been at it since dawn. | {m7=work} Restday's for those who can afford it. | {m7=work} Someone has to keep the fires in.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_rest_restless
when concept=moment.reply_day conv.m7o=rest self.drive=restless|ambitious
does answer.how
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say {m7=joke} I hate Restdays. Nothing gets done. | {m7=joke} I've tidied the house twice. | {m7=joke} Tomorrow can't come soon enough.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_dawn
when concept=moment.reply_day conv.m7o=dawn
does answer.how
priority 1
say {m7=dawn} Birds have the right idea. They sing about it. | {m7=dawn} Don't. I've not woken up yet. | {m7=dawn} Ask me after I've eaten. | {m7=dawn} Same sack, different day.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_dusk
when concept=moment.reply_day conv.m7o=dusk
does answer.how
priority 1
say And not before time. | Supper and my own chair. I can taste it. | Best hour of the day, this. | Another one done, and nothing broken.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_dusk_old
when concept=moment.reply_day conv.m7o=dusk self.stage=old
does answer.how
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say At my age you're glad of every one. | Days go quicker the fewer you've got. | I watched the sun down. I always do.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_night
when concept=moment.reply_day conv.m7o=night
does answer.how
priority 1
say {m7=night} Couldn't sleep. | {m7=night} Walking it off. | {m7=night} I could ask you the same. | {m7=night} Better out here than staring at the rafters.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_night_young
when concept=moment.reply_day conv.m7o=night self.stage=young|adolescent
does answer.how
priority 1
say {m7=joke} Don't tell my mum. | {m7=joke} I'm going home. I'm going right now. | {m7=joke} I heard a noise and came to look.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_crowd
when concept=moment.reply_day conv.m7o=crowd
does answer.how
priority 1
say {m7=market} Every village for a day's walk, by the look of it. | {m7=market} Keep your tail tucked in. | {m7=market} I've been trodden on twice.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_crowd_nervy
when concept=moment.reply_day conv.m7o=crowd self.temper=nervy
does answer.how
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say {m7=crowd} Too many. Far too many. I can't breathe. | {m7=crowd} Everyone's treading on my tail. | {m7=crowd} I'm going home. I'll come back when it thins.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_quiet
when concept=moment.reply_day conv.m7o=quiet
does answer.how
priority 1
say Indoors, with any sense. | Suits me. | Don't complain. You'll bring the crowds. | Gone to the next town, I expect. Something's always better there.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_done
when concept=moment.reply_day conv.m7o=done
does answer.how
priority 1
say {m7=done} Off home with you, then. | {m7=done} Lucky. I've half a day yet. | {m7=done} Put your feet up. You've earned it.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_done_too
when concept=moment.reply_day conv.m7o=done self.shift=after
does answer.how
priority 1
say {m7=both} Me too. Shall we find a bench? | {m7=both} Same. My back's made of wood. | {m7=both} Done and dusted. Let's not talk about it.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_dayoff
when concept=moment.reply_day conv.m7o=dayoff
does answer.how
priority 1
say {m7=dayoff} Enjoy it. Don't waste it on the likes of me. | {m7=dayoff} Make the most of it. | {m7=dayoff} Lucky beast. | {m7=dayoff} You'll have forgotten nothing. That's the feeling of rest.
then other: moment.close

# As they are, whatever the opener (priority 1, so they stand with the keyed answers).

rule m7_day_re_guard
when concept=moment.reply_day self.on_watch=yes
does answer.how
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say {m7=work} Can't stop. I'm on watch. | {m7=work} Long one. Ask me at the end of it. | {m7=work} Quiet so far. Don't say it. You'll jinx it.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_tired
when concept=moment.reply_day self.tired=yes
does answer.how
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say {m7=weary} I'm that #tired# I could sleep on a fence. | {m7=weary} I could sleep standing, like a horse. | {m7=weary} Don't ask. I'll cry.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_hungry
when concept=moment.reply_day self.hungry=yes
does answer.how
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say {m7=hungry} I'll tell you after I've eaten. | {m7=hungry} I'm #hungry#. That's my whole day. | {m7=hungry} My belly's been talking louder than me.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_chatty
when concept=moment.reply_day self.talk=chatty
does answer.how
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say {m7=gossip} Never mind that. You'll never guess who I saw at the well. | {m7=gossip} Oh, that reminds me. Have you heard about the baker's cart? | {m7=gossip} Listen, I've news. Sit down a moment.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_rich
when concept=moment.reply_day self.wealth=rich self.stage=adult|old !conv.m7o
does answer.how
cooldown 2d
say {m7=posh} Pleasant enough. Calls and letters. | {m7=posh} A dull dinner, and a duller visit after it. | {m7=posh} One does what one must.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_day_re_mourning
when concept=moment.reply_day self.mourning=kin|friend
does answer.how
priority 2
cooldown 1d
say {k=grief} I get through them. That's all. | {k=grief} Every day's long, this week. | {k=grief} I keep thinking I'll tell them about it.
