# ================================================================ Festivals: openers (here.festival is the festival's
# name, today's or the one coming)

rule m7_fest_open_today
when concept=talk.festival topic.when=today here.festival
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say #greet#, and a happy #here.festival#! | #here.festival.capitalize# at last. | You've a ribbon on, I see. Proper #here.festival# spirit. | Smell that? That's a feast cooking.
then other: moment.reply_festival

rule m7_fest_open_soon
when concept=talk.festival topic.when=soon here.festival
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say #here.festival.capitalize#'s nearly on us. | Ready for #here.festival#? | Not long now till #here.festival#. | They've asked me to bring a pie for #here.festival#. Me! I burn water.
then other: moment.reply_festival

rule m7_fest_open_today_spring
when concept=talk.festival topic.when=today here.season=spring
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say Blossom in every doorway. | They've hung green boughs over the gate. | First feast after the lean months. My belly cheered.
then other: moment.reply_festival

rule m7_fest_open_today_summer
when concept=talk.festival topic.when=today here.season=summer
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say They'll dance till the light goes, and it goes late. | The fires'll be lit at dusk. | Too hot to dance. They'll dance anyway.
then other: moment.reply_festival

rule m7_fest_open_today_autumn
when concept=talk.festival topic.when=today here.season=autumn
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say The last of it's in. Now we eat it. | Corn dollies on every door. | Bread, cider, more bread. That's the plan.
then other: moment.reply_festival

rule m7_fest_open_today_winter
when concept=talk.festival topic.when=today here.season=winter
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say Dark early, and every window lit. | Look at it. Candles in every house. | The cold can't get in tonight. Not with all those fires.
then other: moment.reply_festival

rule m7_fest_open_soon_poor
when concept=talk.festival topic.when=soon self.wealth=destitute|poor self.stage=adult|old
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
priority 1
say {m7o=need} How's a body to feast on nothing? | {m7o=need} Everyone in new ribbons, and me in last year's coat. | {m7o=need} Festivals are for those with full purses.
then other: moment.reply_festival

rule m7_fest_open_soon_cook
when concept=talk.festival topic.when=soon self.job=cook|baker|innkeeper|brewer
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say {m7o=busy} I'll be baking from tonight till it's over. | {m7o=busy} Three days' work for one day's feast. | {m7o=busy} Order your pies now or go without.
then other: moment.reply_festival

rule m7_fest_open_young_today
when concept=talk.festival topic.when=today self.stage=young
does ask.detail
cooldown 1d
say {m7o=pup} Is it the feast now? Is it? | {m7o=pup} Will there be honey cakes? Say there will. | {m7o=pup} I'm going to stay up till the end. All of it.
then other: moment.reply_festival

rule m7_fest_open_young_soon
when concept=talk.festival topic.when=soon self.stage=young here.festival
does ask.detail
cooldown 1d
say {m7o=pup} How many sleeps till #here.festival#? | {m7o=pup} Will there be honey cakes? Say there will. | {m7o=pup} Is it #here.festival# tomorrow? Is it?
then other: moment.reply_festival

# ================================================================ Festivals: answers

rule m7_fest_re_any
when concept=moment.reply_festival
does answer.plan
say {m7=glad} Wouldn't miss it for all the #money# in Ridgemere. | {m7=glad} I've my good coat brushed and ready. | {m7=glad} Aye. Eat, dance, regret it in the morning. | {m7=glad} It comes round quicker every year. | {m7=glad} I'll be there. Somewhere near the food.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_fest_re_any2
when concept=moment.reply_festival
does answer.plan
say Same as every year, and I'll love it the same. | Bright One, the noise there'll be. | They'd better not run out of cider like last time.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_fest_re_priest
when concept=moment.reply_festival self.job=priest
does answer.plan
cooldown 1d
say Remember why we keep it, between the cups. | I've the blessing to say. Pray they listen. | The chapel first, then the feast. That's the order.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_fest_re_guard
when concept=moment.reply_festival self.job=guard|soldier
does answer.plan
cooldown 1d
say {m7=work} I'm on duty. Somebody's got to fish the drunks out of the trough. | {m7=work} Double watch. Every festival, the same fights. | {m7=work} I'll hear it from the wall. Lovely.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_fest_re_cook
when concept=moment.reply_festival self.job=cook|baker|innkeeper|brewer
does answer.plan
cooldown 1d
say {m7=work} I'll be feeding the lot of you. Don't expect me to dance. | {m7=work} Every oven in town's going. | {m7=work} I've not seen my bed since yesterday.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_fest_re_merchant
when concept=moment.reply_festival self.role=merchant
does answer.plan
cooldown 1d
say Best trade of the season. Ribbons sell themselves. | I've laid in triple stock. Pray I sell it. | Festivals are good to merchants. Very good.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_fest_re_poor
when concept=moment.reply_festival self.wealth=destitute|poor self.stage=adult|old
does answer.plan
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say {m7=poor} I'll watch. Watching's free. | {m7=poor} The chapel feeds folk at festival. I'll be in the line. | {m7=poor} Not this year. Maybe next.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_fest_re_rich
when concept=moment.reply_festival self.wealth=rich self.stage=adult|old
does answer.plan
cooldown 1d
say {m7=posh} We'll give a little something to the town, of course. | {m7=posh} I've a dinner to host. Twelve at table. Exhausting. | {m7=posh} I've ordered more candles than the chapel.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_fest_re_house
when concept=moment.reply_festival self.house self.wealth=rich
does answer.plan
cooldown 2d
say {m7=posh} Our House always puts on a show. It's expected. | {m7=posh} Father wants the whole hall lit. Every candle in the city. | {m7=posh} The Council will be watching who gives most. As ever.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_fest_re_mourning
when concept=moment.reply_festival self.mourning=kin|friend
does answer.plan
priority 2
cooldown 1d
say {k=grief} I'll not go this year. | {k=grief} They loved this festival. I can't face it. | {k=grief} Maybe I'll sit at the back. Maybe.
then other: keeping.sorry

rule m7_fest_re_old
when concept=moment.reply_festival self.stage=old
does answer.plan
cooldown 1d
say In my day it went three days, not one. | I've danced at sixty of them. I'll sit this one out. Maybe. | They don't sing the old songs any more. Nobody knows them.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_fest_re_young
when concept=moment.reply_festival self.stage=young
does answer.plan
cooldown 1d
say {m7=glad} I'm going to eat six honey cakes. Six! | {m7=glad} Can I stay up? Can I? | {m7=glad} I've practised the dance. Watch! No, watch!
then other: moment.close

rule m7_fest_re_adolescent
when concept=moment.reply_festival self.stage=adolescent
does answer.plan
cooldown 1d
say {m7=teen} There's dancing after dark. Everyone's going. Everyone. | {m7=teen} I'm not wearing that ribbon. I'm not. | {m7=teen} Maybe someone'll ask me to dance. Maybe.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_fest_re_from_away
when concept=moment.reply_festival self.from!=ridgemere here.region=ridgemere
does answer.plan
cooldown 2d
say {m7=home} At home we do it different. More singing, less shoving. | {m7=home} It's not the same as at home. Bigger, but not the same. | {m7=home} Back home they'll be setting the long table about now.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_fest_re_short
when concept=moment.reply_festival self.temper=short
does answer.plan
cooldown 1d
say {m7=joke} Noise, drink and fools. I'll stay in. | {m7=joke} Wake me when it's over. | {m7=joke} Every year someone's sick on my step.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_fest_re_devout
when concept=moment.reply_festival self.piety=devout
does answer.plan
cooldown 1d
say I'll be at the chapel first. Give thanks before you feast. | It's a holy day before it's a drinking one. | I've a candle ready for the window.
then other: moment.close

# To a pup's festival questions (m7o=pup).

rule m7_fest_re_to_pup_today
when concept=moment.reply_festival conv.m7o=pup topic.when=today self.stage=adult|old
does answer.plan
priority 3
say {m7=topup} Cakes, and dancing, and a bonfire. If you're good. | {m7=topup} Stay by your mother in the crowd, mind. | {m7=topup} Till the end? We'll see who's asleep first. | {m7=topup} It's today, you daft pup. Go and find the cakes.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_fest_re_to_pup_soon
when concept=moment.reply_festival conv.m7o=pup topic.when=soon self.stage=adult|old
does answer.plan
priority 3
say {m7=topup} Not long. A few more sleeps. | {m7=topup} Soon. Be good till then and there might be cakes. | {m7=topup} Ask me again tomorrow, and the day after. Then it'll be here.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_fest_re_pup_pup
when concept=moment.reply_festival conv.m7o=pup self.stage=young|adolescent
does answer.plan
priority 3
say {m7=pupchat} I'm having two! | {m7=pupchat} My big sister says there's a fire as high as a house. | {m7=pupchat} I'm going to dance with everyone.
then other: moment.close

# ================================================================ Lore: openers (talk.lore: the realm's tales, by anyone)

rule m7_lore_open_any
when concept=talk.lore
does tell.story
cooldown 1d
say {m7o=tale} My grandmother used to say the hills were sleeping giants. | {m7o=tale} They say a giant dragged one claw from Glasswater to the sea, and that's the Long River. | {m7o=tale} They say the old roads were laid by wolves who never slept. | {m7o=tale} Put your ear to the ground on a still night, they say, and you'll hear the dead talking.
then other: moment.reply_lore

rule m7_lore_open_night
when concept=talk.lore here.time=night|dusk
does tell.story
cooldown 1d
say {m7o=tale} Don't whistle after dark. It calls things. | {m7o=tale} Count the stars and you'll go blind, my mother said. | {m7o=tale} They say a shiver at dusk means someone's stepped where you'll be buried. | {m7o=tale} Never answer a voice in the dark that knows your name.
then other: moment.reply_lore

rule m7_lore_open_wardens
when concept=talk.lore
does tell.story
cooldown 2d
say {m7o=tale} Folk say the Wardens watch the Quickened from somewhere past the mountains. | {m7o=tale} Ever seen a Warden? My uncle swore he did. Grey cloak, no face. | {m7o=tale} If you've a gift, they say, the Wardens hear of it.
then other: moment.reply_lore

rule m7_lore_open_houses
when concept=talk.lore here.region=ridgemere
does tell.story
cooldown 2d
say {m7o=tale} They say the first Greatly came down from the hills with a trowel and a bag of lime. | {m7o=tale} They say the cellars under Grayrock Hall go down under the sea and never stop. | {m7o=tale} They say there was a fifth House once, and the other four swore never to speak its name.
then other: moment.reply_lore

rule m7_lore_open_old
when concept=talk.lore self.stage=old
does tell.story
cooldown 2d
say {m7o=tale} When I was a pup they said the winters were longer because the wolves were kinder. | {m7o=tale} My gran told me a comet came in her girlhood and burned the sky a week. | {m7o=tale} My father swore the old well spoke to him, the night before the flood.
then other: moment.reply_lore

rule m7_lore_open_young
when concept=talk.lore self.stage=young
does ask.detail
cooldown 1d
say {m7o=pup} Is it true there's a dragon under the hill? | {m7o=pup} Is there really a wolf with no shadow that walks the roads at night? | {m7o=pup} Do the dead come back on the longest night? Brindle says so.
then other: moment.reply_lore

# ================================================================ Lore: answers (to a tale told, m7o=tale)

rule m7_lore_re_any
when concept=moment.reply_lore
does react.story
say {m7=scoff} Every grandmother says that. | {m7=scoff} Who told you that? | {m7=scoff} Old tales have a grain of something in them. Not much.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_lore_re_any2
when concept=moment.reply_lore
does react.story
say {m7=believe} My mother told it the same. Word for word. | {m7=believe} Don't. I'll never sleep. | {m7=believe} Hush. Somebody'll hear. | {m7=believe} That's nonsense, and I believe every word.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_lore_re_any3
when concept=moment.reply_lore
does react.story
say {m7=version} I heard it different. Worse, my version. | {m7=version} That's not how my gran told it. Hers had a fox in it. | {m7=version} You've left the best bit out.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_lore_re_frank
when concept=moment.reply_lore self.honesty=frank
does react.story
cooldown 1d
say {m7=scoff} #nonsense.capitalize#. Pure #nonsense#. | {m7=scoff} Tales are for pups and drunks. | {m7=scoff} I'll believe it when it pays my rent.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_lore_re_devout
when concept=moment.reply_lore self.piety=devout
does react.story
cooldown 1d
say {m7=pious} The Bright One made the world. The rest is gossip. | {m7=pious} Don't speak lightly of such things. | {m7=pious} There's more under the sky than the priests tell us. I'll grant that.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_lore_re_old
when concept=moment.reply_lore self.stage=old
does react.story
cooldown 1d
say {m7=oldtell} That's not how it goes. Sit down, I'll tell it right. | {m7=oldtell} I knew a wolf who knew a wolf who was there. | {m7=oldtell} They told it better when I was young. Slower.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_lore_re_young
when concept=moment.reply_lore self.stage=young
does react.story
cooldown 1d
say {m7=believe} Is that true? Truly true? | {m7=believe} I'm not scared. I'm just going to stand behind you. | {m7=believe} Tell it again! The scary bit!
then other: moment.close

rule m7_lore_re_scholar
when concept=moment.reply_lore self.job=scholar|priest|official
does react.story
cooldown 1d
say {m7=scholar} There's something like it in the old rolls, if you can read the hand. | {m7=scholar} The records say something of the kind. Duller, mind. | {m7=scholar} Tales grow in the telling. The truth's usually smaller.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_lore_re_nervy
when concept=moment.reply_lore self.temper=nervy here.time=night|dusk
does react.story ask.opinion
cooldown 1d
say {m7=spooked} Why would you say that? Now? Here? | {m7=spooked} I'm going home. Right now. With a lamp. | {m7=spooked} Did you hear that? Behind us?
then other: moment.close

# From elsewhere: each country's way of telling it (never said at home, where everyone tells it so).

rule m7_lore_re_from_frost
when concept=moment.reply_lore self.from=frosthollow here.region!=frosthollow
does react.story
cooldown 2d
say {m7=hometale} Up the valley they'd say it's the mountain breathing. Everything's the mountain, with us. | {m7=hometale} We've a tale like it. Ends with a cave-in. They all do. | {m7=hometale} In Frosthollow we'd knock on the mine door for luck before we said that aloud.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_lore_re_from_cold
when concept=moment.reply_lore self.from=coldwater here.region!=coldwater
does react.story
cooldown 2d
say {m7=hometale} At Coldwater we'd say the lake knows. The lake knows everything. | {m7=hometale} My grandfather would throw a fish back for saying that. | {m7=hometale} There's a tale like it about Glasswater. Colder, mind.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_lore_re_from_oak
when concept=moment.reply_lore self.from=oakhaven here.region!=oakhaven
does react.story
cooldown 2d
say {m7=hometale} In the Rainwood we'd say an oak saw it. Oaks see everything. | {m7=hometale} We tell that one round the fire at story night. Better, mind. | {m7=hometale} My granddam told it with a ghost in it. Always a ghost, in Oakhaven.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_lore_re_from_mire
when concept=moment.reply_lore self.from=mirebridge|fenshore here.region!=fens
does react.story
cooldown 2d
say {m7=hometale} In the fens we'd say: don't follow the lights. That's the end of every tale. | {m7=hometale} Fen folk know a dozen like it, and every one's true. Mostly. | {m7=hometale} My aunt would spit three times and touch iron.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_lore_re_from_lark
when concept=moment.reply_lore self.from=larkfield here.region!=larkfield
does react.story
cooldown 2d
say {m7=hometale} A carter told me that one at home. Taller, it was. | {m7=hometale} In Larkfield you'd pay a penny for a tale like that, and get change. | {m7=hometale} Every tale passes through Larkfield sooner or later. That one came back muddier.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_lore_re_from_south
when concept=moment.reply_lore self.from=southmeadow here.region!=southmeadow
does react.story
cooldown 2d
say {m7=hometale} Down south we'd tell that at harvest, with the cider going round. | {m7=hometale} Every field in Southmeadow has its story. That's a field tale if ever I heard one. | {m7=hometale} We'd say a scarecrow saw it. Don't laugh.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_lore_re_from_salt
when concept=moment.reply_lore self.from=saltwell here.region!=waste
does react.story
cooldown 2d
say {m7=hometale} In Saltwell we'd tell that at the well, after dark, with the stars out. | {m7=hometale} At home that tale has a hawk in it. Every good tale does. | {m7=hometale} My grandmother told it better, and slower. In the Waste nobody hurries a story.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_lore_re_from_city
when concept=moment.reply_lore self.from=ridgemere here.region!=ridgemere
does react.story
cooldown 2d
say {m7=hometale} In the city they'd say it was a House that did it. It's always a House. | {m7=hometale} We've a tale like that in Ridgemere. Ends with somebody owing money. | {m7=hometale} City folk don't believe tales. We believe rumours. Different thing.
then other: moment.close

# To a pup's question (m7o=pup).

rule m7_lore_re_to_pup
when concept=moment.reply_lore conv.m7o=pup self.stage=adult|old
does react.story
priority 3
say {m7=topup} Only for pups who stay up late. So don't. | {m7=topup} Who's been filling your head? ...No. Probably not. | {m7=topup} Ask your gran. She'll tell it scarier than me. | {m7=topup} Not round here. The watch wouldn't stand for it.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_lore_re_to_pup_old
when concept=moment.reply_lore conv.m7o=pup self.stage=old
does react.story
priority 3
cooldown 1d
say {m7=topup} Sit down, pup, and I'll tell you the whole of it. | {m7=topup} When I was your size, we were told the same. And I'm still here. | {m7=topup} There is. And it likes pups who don't do as they're told.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_lore_re_pup_pup
when concept=moment.reply_lore conv.m7o=pup self.stage=young|adolescent
does react.story
priority 3
say {m7=pupchat} Brindle says a lot of things. | {m7=pupchat} I'm not scared. You're scared. | {m7=pupchat} Let's go and look! ...Tomorrow. In the day.
then other: moment.close

# ================================================================ Where you're from (talk.accent): b's voice noticed

rule m7_acc_open_any
when concept=talk.accent
does ask.whereabouts
cooldown 1d
say Where's that voice from? | I can't place your voice. Where's it from? | Say that again. I like how you say it. | #surprise#! There's a voice from somewhere.
then other: moment.reply_home

rule m7_acc_open_rude
when concept=talk.accent self.warmth=cold
does ask.detail
cooldown 2d
say Can't understand a word you say. | Talk properly, will you? | Where'd you learn to talk like that? A barn?
then other: moment.reply_home

rule m7_acc_open_warm
when concept=talk.accent self.warmth=warm
does ask.detail
cooldown 2d
say I love that voice. Where's it from? | You've a lovely way of talking. Like music. | Go on, say something else. I could listen all day.
then other: moment.reply_home

rule m7_acc_open_young
when concept=talk.accent self.stage=young
does ask.detail
cooldown 1d
say Why do you talk funny? | Say something else! You talk like a story. | Are you from far away? Really far?
then other: moment.reply_home

rule m7_acc_open_city
when concept=talk.accent here.region=ridgemere self.from=ridgemere
does ask.detail
cooldown 2d
say Fresh off the road, are you? | You'll lose that voice in a year. The city wears it off. | That's never a city voice. I can always tell.
then other: moment.reply_home

rule m7_acc_open_merchant
when concept=talk.accent self.role=merchant
does ask.detail
cooldown 2d
say A #topic.accent_town# voice! I had a carter from there once. Never paid me. | I'd know that voice in a crowd. Your folk come to my stall. | #topic.accent_town#, is it? I'll mind my weights, then.
then other: moment.reply_home

# Answers about home (self is the one whose voice was noticed; topic.accent_town is where they grew up). One answering
# where they stand at home (the one who asked is the stranger) answers that, first.

rule m7_home_re_any
when concept=moment.reply_home self.home_here!=yes
does answer.detail
say {m7=home} #topic.accent_town#, born and bred. | {m7=home} #topic.accent_town#, if you must know. | {m7=home} From #topic.accent_town#. It shows, does it? | {m7=home} #topic.accent_town#. I'll die talking like it.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_home_re_frost
when concept=moment.reply_home self.from=frosthollow
does answer.detail
priority 1
say {m7=home} Frosthollow. Up the Pass Road, under the Whitefangs. Where the snow lives. | {m7=home} The valley. Frosthollow. We say what we mean, and not much of it. | {m7=home} Miner's voice, that. Frosthollow. Grew up by lamplight.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_home_re_cold
when concept=moment.reply_home self.from=coldwater
does answer.detail
priority 1
say {m7=home} Coldwater. On Glasswater, under the mountains. You'd love it. Or freeze. | {m7=home} Lake country. We talk slow. The fish don't hurry, why should we? | {m7=home} Coldwater. I can still smell the reeds when I close my eyes.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_home_re_oak
when concept=moment.reply_home self.from=oakhaven
does answer.detail
priority 1
say {m7=home} Oakhaven. The Rainwood. Green all summer, and then some. | {m7=home} From under the oaks. We take our time, in Oakhaven. | {m7=home} The Rainwood, aye. Slow talk from a slow wood.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_home_re_mire
when concept=moment.reply_home self.from=mirebridge|fenshore
does answer.detail
priority 1
say {m7=home} #self.from.capitalize#. The fens. Wet feet, and a wetter voice. | {m7=home} Fen-born. The Sallow Fens. Wet feet and long memories. | {m7=home} #self.from.capitalize#. Don't make the face. Everyone makes the face.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_home_re_lark
when concept=moment.reply_home self.from=larkfield
does answer.detail
priority 1
say {m7=home} Larkfield. The downs. I was raised shouting prices over sheep. | {m7=home} Larkfield. Every carter in the realm drinks in our inn. | {m7=home} The Larkdowns. Wide skies, quick tongues.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_home_re_south
when concept=moment.reply_home self.from=southmeadow
does answer.detail
priority 1
say {m7=home} Southmeadow! Orchards and cider and sun on your back. Why did I leave? | {m7=home} The far south. Southmeadow. We grow your bread. | {m7=home} Southmeadow. Where the apples come from. You're welcome.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_home_re_city
when concept=moment.reply_home self.from=ridgemere
does answer.detail
priority 1
say {m7=home} Ridgemere. The city. Rain and Houses and too many stairs. | {m7=home} City-born. You can't scrub it off. | {m7=home} Ridgemere. Don't hold it against me.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_home_re_broad_old
when concept=moment.reply_home self.accent=broad self.stage=old
does answer.detail
cooldown 1d
say {m7=home} #topic.accent_town# through and through. Seventy years of it. | {m7=home} My voice never left home, and nor did I till now. | {m7=home} They'll bury me sounding like #topic.accent_town#. And proud.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_home_re_defensive
when concept=moment.reply_home self.temper=short
does answer.detail ask.detail
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say {m7=prickly} What of it? | {m7=prickly} I talk how I talk. You talk like a gate hinge. | {m7=prickly} #topic.accent_town#. Got a problem with that?
then other: moment.close

rule m7_home_re_shy
when concept=moment.reply_home self.tone=shy
does answer.detail
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say {m7=home} Oh. Is it that plain? #topic.accent_town#. Sorry. | {m7=home} I try to talk like you lot. It doesn't take. | {m7=home} #topic.accent_town#. I don't, um. I don't say much, usually.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_home_re_young
when concept=moment.reply_home self.stage=young|adolescent
does answer.detail
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say {m7=home} #topic.accent_town#. We're only visiting. | {m7=home} I'm from #topic.accent_town#! Everyone talks like this there. | {m7=home} I don't talk funny. You do.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_home_re_homesick
when concept=moment.reply_home self.warmth=warm self.stage=adult|old
does answer.detail
cooldown 2d
say {m7=home} #topic.accent_town#. I miss it every day. Some days more. | {m7=home} I left for work. I'll go back for good one day. | {m7=home} You'd like it there. Everyone does. Except me, apparently, since I left.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_home_re_glad_gone
when concept=moment.reply_home self.drive=restless|ambitious self.stage=adult|old
does answer.detail
cooldown 2d
say {m7=gladgone} #topic.accent_town#. And glad to be shot of it. | {m7=gladgone} Nothing ever happens in #topic.accent_town#. That's why I'm here. | {m7=gladgone} I left as soon as I could walk the road.
then other: moment.close

# At home: the one asking is the stranger here (priority 2, before all the rest).

rule m7_home_re_local_any
when concept=moment.reply_home self.home_here=yes
does answer.detail
priority 1
say {m7=local} From here, as it happens. You're standing in it. | {m7=local} Born and raised right here. It's you that's the stranger. | {m7=local} Here. I've never lived anywhere else.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_home_re_local_ridgemere
when concept=moment.reply_home self.from=ridgemere here.region=ridgemere
does answer.detail
priority 2
say {m7=local} Ridgemere, friend. You're standing in it. It's your voice that's the odd one. | {m7=local} Born three streets over. You're the one with the accent, here. | {m7=local} From here. Every wolf on this street sounds like me.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_home_re_local_frosthollow
when concept=moment.reply_home self.from=frosthollow here.region=frosthollow
does answer.detail
priority 2
say {m7=local} From here. Where else? You're the one off the Pass Road. | {m7=local} Frosthollow. You're in it. Mind the ice. | {m7=local} This is a Frosthollow voice, in Frosthollow. Yours is the strange one.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_home_re_local_coldwater
when concept=moment.reply_home self.from=coldwater here.region=coldwater
does answer.detail
priority 2
say {m7=local} I'm from here, friend. You're the one with the voice. | {m7=local} Coldwater, born on the shore yonder. You'll be the stranger. | {m7=local} Everyone on the lake talks like me. Give it a week.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_home_re_local_oakhaven
when concept=moment.reply_home self.from=oakhaven here.region=oakhaven
does answer.detail
priority 2
say {m7=local} From here. Oakhaven, under these very oaks. It's you that's foreign. | {m7=local} This is how we talk in the Rainwood. You'll catch it. | {m7=local} Born a stone's throw off. You're the one from away.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_home_re_local_mirebridge
when concept=moment.reply_home self.from=mirebridge|fenshore here.region=fens
does answer.detail
priority 2
say {m7=local} You're in the fens, friend. This is how the fens talk. | {m7=local} #here.town#. Here. You'll be from away, no? | {m7=local} My voice is at home. It's yours that's wandered.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_home_re_local_larkfield
when concept=moment.reply_home self.from=larkfield here.region=larkfield
does answer.detail
priority 2
say {m7=local} Larkfield, and you're in it. It's you that talks funny, here. | {m7=local} Every stall on the downs talks like me. | {m7=local} Born here, sold here, I'll be buried here. You're the stranger.
then other: moment.close

rule m7_home_re_local_southmeadow
when concept=moment.reply_home self.from=southmeadow here.region=southmeadow
does answer.detail
priority 2
say {m7=local} Southmeadow, and you're standing in it! It's your voice that's the odd one. | {m7=local} From here, my apple. Everyone talks like this in the orchards. | {m7=local} I'm the one at home. You'll be from away.
then other: moment.close
